{"id":"lycian-way","title":"Lycian Way","who":"Classic route · Türkiye's Mediterranean coast on foot","when":"March–May and September–November","vehicle":"On foot, 2–5 weeks (or highlights in a week)","kind":"walk","color":"#0284c7","summary":"About 540 km of old mule paths and Roman roads along the Turquoise Coast from Fethiye towards Antalya: cliff paths above turquoise bays, the ruins of Lycian cities, rock tombs and sunken Kekova, with village pensions and camping. Hot in summer; spring and autumn are best.","sources":[{"label":"The Gone Goat: hiking the Lycian Way in a week","url":"https://www.thegonegoat.com/turkey/hiking-the-lycian-way-turkey"},{"label":"Novo-Monde: the Lycian Way from Fethiye to Kabak","url":"https://www.novo-monde.com/en/lycian-way-fethiye-kabak/"}],"approximate":"Main stages from Ölüdeniz to Çıralı; the line follows paths near the marked trail.","km":255,"bbox":[29.1162,36.1529,30.482,36.5709],"stops":[{"name":"Ölüdeniz","place":"Ölüdeniz, Fethiye","at":[36.5709,29.1403],"text":"The famous blue lagoon at the start, paragliders overhead.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Paragliding_view_oludeniz_-_panoramio_%282%29.jpg/500px-Paragliding_view_oludeniz_-_panoramio_%282%29.jpg","page":"Ölüdeniz","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paragliding_view_oludeniz_-_panoramio_%282%29.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Faralya","place":"Faralya, Fethiye","at":[36.482,29.1188],"text":"High above Butterfly Valley, a gorge running down to a hidden beach.","source":{"label":"Novo-Monde: Fethiye to Kabak","url":"https://www.novo-monde.com/en/lycian-way-fethiye-kabak/"}},{"name":"Kabak","place":"Kabak, Fethiye","at":[36.462,29.1259],"text":"A wild bay of tree-house camps and yoga retreats."},{"name":"Alınca","place":"Alınca, Muğla","at":[36.4478,29.1431],"text":"A cliff-top hamlet with one of the trail's great views."},{"name":"Patara","place":"Patara, Antalya","at":[3